Java 8 Built-in Functional Interfaces (in java.util.function)

Java 8 introduced standard functional interfaces

Here are the main four, often remembered as the “Big 4”:

🧠 1. Function<T, R>

📘 Purpose: Takes one input (T) → returns a result (R)

Function<Integer, String> f = n -> "Value is " + n;
System.out.println(f.apply(10)); // Output: Value is 10


🧠 Layman: “I give you something, you give me something back.”

🧠 2. Predicate<T>

📘 Purpose: Takes one input (T) → returns boolean

Predicate<Integer> isEven = n -> n % 2 == 0;
System.out.println(isEven.test(10)); // true
System.out.println(isEven.test(7));  // false


🧠 Layman: “You give me something, I’ll say true or false.”

✅ Common use: filtering, validation, conditions

🧠 3. Supplier<T>

📘 Purpose: Takes no input, returns a value (T)

Supplier<Double> randomValue = () -> Math.random();
System.out.println(randomValue.get()); // Example: 0.457892


🧠 Layman: “I don’t need anything from you — I’ll just give you something.”

✅ Common use: random values, object creation, config data

🧠 4. Consumer<T>

📘 Purpose: Takes one input (T) → returns nothing

Consumer<String> printer = name -> System.out.println("Hello, " + name);
printer.accept("Murali"); // Output: Hello, Murali


🧠 Layman: “You give me something, and I’ll just use it — I won’t return anything.”

✅ Common use: logging, printing, saving to DB, etc.




| Interface    | Analogy                                                                 |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Function`   | Like a **machine**: you give input, it gives output 🎰                  |
| `Predicate`  | Like a **judge**: says true/false ⚖️                                    |
| `Supplier`   | Like a **vending machine**: gives you an item without input 🥤          |
| `Consumer`   | Like a **trash bin**: accepts something and doesn’t return anything 🗑️  |
| `Runnable`   | Like a **task runner**: just runs 🚀                                    |
| `Callable`   | Like a **task runner that returns result** 🧾                           |
| `Comparator` | Like a **referee**: decides who’s greater 🏁                            |

| Interface          | Package              | Method              | Input | Output        | Use                |
| ------------------ | -------------------- | ------------------- | ----- | ------------- | ------------------ |
| **Function<T, R>** | `java.util.function` | `R apply(T t)`      | Yes   | Yes           | Transform data     |
| **Predicate<T>**   | `java.util.function` | `boolean test(T t)` | Yes   | Yes (boolean) | Filter / condition |
| **Consumer<T>**    | `java.util.function` | `void accept(T t)`  | Yes   | No            | Perform an action  |
| **Supplier<T>**    | `java.util.function` | `T get()`           | No    | Yes           | Provide data       |

